  "id": "COMPOUND:33008 - PROTEIN:5427",
  "verbalization": "Isofurcatain is implicated in the biological activity of KYSE-180 cells through a multi-step mechanism involving the NQO1 protein. The evidence suggests that Isofurcatain directly targets NQO1, which is then a target of Scoparic Acid A, another compound that is also a target of Isofurcatain. This creates a chain of targets that ultimately leads to the interaction with KYSE-180 cells. The presence of multiple targets along this pathway, coupled with the high confidence scores in the relationships, indicates a potential role for Isofurcatain in modulating NQO1 activity, which may influence cellular processes in KYSE-180 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, emphasizing the importance of NQO1 as a central mediator in the effects of Isofurcatain on KYSE-180.",
